#nexus [SplitsTree6]

BEGIN SPLITSTREE6;
DIMENSIONS nDataNodes=11 nAlgorithms=9;
PROGRAM version='SplitsTree App (version 6.5.1-j7, built 23 Sep 2025)';
WORKFLOW creationDate='1758674293063'; [Wed Sep 24 09:38:13 JST 2025]
END; [SPLITSTREE6]

[
Methods:
Analysis was performed using SplitsTree App 6.0.0 (Huson and Bryant 2024).
The original input consisted of 15 taxa and a 15 x 15 distance matrix.
The Neighbor Net method (Bryant & Moulton 2004, Bryant & Huson 2023) was used (default options) so as to obtain 28 splits, cyclic.
The Network Pruning method (Hayamisu) was used (default options) so as to obtain 19 nodes and 21 edges.
The Razor Net method was used (default options) so as to obtain 19 nodes and 21 edges.
The Show Splits method was used (default options) so as to obtain a Split Network visualization.

References:
Bryant & Huson 2023: D. Bryant and DH Huson, NeighborNet- improved algorithms and implementation. Front. Bioinform. 3, 2023.
Bryant & Moulton 2004: D. Bryant and V. Moulton. Neighbor-net: An agglomerative method for the construction of phylogenetic networks. Molecular Biology and Evolution, 21(2):255– 265, 2004.
Hayamisu: M. Hayamisu et al, in preparation, 2025.
Huson and Bryant 2024: D.H. Huson and D. Bryant. The SplitsTree App: interactive analysis and visualization using phylogenetic trees and networks. Nature Methods, 2024.
]

BEGIN TAXA;
TITLE 'Input Taxa';
LINK ALGORITHM = 'Input Data Loader';
DIMENSIONS ntax=15;
TAXLABELS
	[1] 't1'
	[2] 't2'
	[3] 't3'
	[4] 't4'
	[5] 't5'
	[6] 't6'
	[7] 't7'
